		(property "Note" "Output daughterboard blade clip, ratified joint 12V (spec Sec 2.8 v1.4.0); mates with the TE 63849-1 tab on the daughterboard side. [2026-07-05 iteration 5: clip part swapped Keystone 3586 (SMD) -> Keystone 3557 bare top-entry clip (THT, UL 30A@500VAC, catalog M55 p.41; LCSC carriage: 3557-10/C3205403 in the fuse-holder category, variant UNVERIFIED -- DigiKey/Mouser carry 3557 directly, consigned fallback; 3586 stays vendored as the SMD fallback pending the OQ-86 sample). Rotated: slot axis perpendicular to the daughterboard wall line, legs ALONG the clip row (3.4mm pitch, verified from the catalog mounting details). Mates the TE 63951-1 right-angle tab descending blade-down from the daughterboard -- see docs/standard-tier-review/blade-fit-check-2026-07-04.md addenda 3-5.] [2026-07-06 iteration 7: mate swapped Keystone 3557 -> TE 63969-1 FASTON .250 PCB receptacle (owner-ratified; the DESIGNED mate for the 63951-1 blade -- 0.81mm thickness at its design centre per rev-E dwg note 3, vertical top entry, 22.9A @30degC rise per TE 108-1706; ORIENTATION per owner: the two O1.40 PCB holes at 5.08mm pitch run PERPENDICULAR to the daughterboard wall line, plan-congruent with the blade tab's own leg holes -- reading chain in blade-fit-check-2026-07-04.md addendum 7; 63968-1 = same-land low-insertion-force fallback; LCSC C2961150 stock ~5 = restock watch, DigiKey depth; Keystone 3557/3586 retired to vendored fallbacks; joint counts re-ratified at 22.9A/125%: 24pin 10, pcie 3/polarity/cable, eps unchanged).]"
